{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וראיתם", :translit "ur'item", :gloss "and you shall see"} {:he "ציצית ביום", :translit "tzitzit ba-yom", :gloss "tzitzit by day"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "וראיתם", :b "ציצית ביום"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "וזכרתם", :translit "uz'khartem", :gloss "and you shall remember"} {:he "והיתה נפש אדוני צרורה בצרור החיים", :translit "v'haytah nefesh adoni tzerurah bitzror ha-chayim", :gloss "and the soul of my lord shall be bound in the bundle of life"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Eight strings correspond to eight limbs (ears, eyes, mouth, nose, hands, feet, genitals, heart) and to eight heavens or eight punishments"}], :frame {:text "The tradition that tzitzit guard a person from transgression is stated at Numbers 15:39 itself. The reward of the soul being bound in the bundle of life is stated at 1 Samuel 25:29. The specific correspondences of strings to limbs, heavens, and punishments appear in midrashic and kabbalistic sources.", :sources ["Numbers 15:39" "1 Samuel 25:29"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ציצית", :translit "tzitzit", :gloss "tzitzit"} {:he "ת\"ר", :translit "tar", :gloss "600 (abbreviated)"} {:he "שמונה חוטין וחמשה קשרים", :translit "shemonah chutin v'chamishah kesherim", :gloss "eight strings and five knots"} {:he "תרי\"ג", :translit "tarig", :gloss "613 (abbreviated)"} {:he "בכל עת יהיו בגדיך לבנים", :translit "b'chol et yihyu begadekha l'vanim", :gloss "at all times your garments shall be white"} {:he "זה ציצית לבגדיכם", :translit "zeh tzitzit l'vadikhem", :gloss "this is tzitzit for your garments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ציצית", :b "ת\"ר"} {:kind :other, :note "600 + 8 strings + 5 knots = 613"} {:kind :gematria, :a "בכל עת יהיו בגדיך לבנים", :b "זה ציצית לבגדיכם"}], :frame {:text "The statement that the commandment of tzitzit is equivalent to all the commandments is found in the Mishnah and elaborated in the Talmud: R. Shimon ben Yochai says this commandment is weighed against all of them. The verse 'at all times your garments shall be white' is from Ecclesiastes 9:8.", :sources ["Menachot 43b" "Ecclesiastes 9:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כל מצות ה'", :translit "kol mitzvot Hashem", :gloss "all the commandments of the LORD"} {:he "תרי\"ב", :translit "tareiv", :gloss "612 (abbreviated)"} {:he "אנכי", :translit "anochi", :gloss "I am"} {:he "ולא יהיה לך", :translit "v'lo yihyeh lekha", :gloss "you shall have no"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כל מצות ה'", :b "תרי\"ב"}], :frame {:text "The tradition that Israel heard the first two commandments, 'I am' and 'You shall have no other gods,' directly from God while Moses transmitted the remaining 612 is found in the Talmud: R. Yehoshua ben Levi says they heard these two from the mouth of the Almighty.", :sources ["Makkot 24a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:a-value 657, :b-value 658, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "ציצית ביום", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "וראיתם"} {:kind :other, :note "Eight strings correspond to eight limbs (ears, eyes, mouth, nose, hands, feet, genitals, heart) and to eight heavens or eight punishments", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ציצית", :a-value 600, :b "ת\"ר", :b-value 600, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "600 + 8 strings + 5 knots = 613", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "בכל עת יהיו בגדיך לבנים", :a-value 724, :b "זה ציצית לבגדיכם", :b-value 721, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "כל מצות ה'", :a-value 591, :b "תרי\"ב", :b-value 612, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:29:20.199517967Z", :model "glm-5.2"}